TITLE
-----
Build Next.js MVP frontend for Internet Banking Concept (login, dashboard, fund transfer, utility payment, user profile)


DESCRIPTION
-----------
Create a new Next.js 14 application at `internet-banking-frontend/` that provides a complete
working demo UI for the existing Spring Boot microservices backend. The app uses NextAuth.js
with the Keycloak OIDC provider for authentication and routes all API calls through the API
gateway at port 8082. Five flows are in scope: login, dashboard, fund transfer, utility
payment, and user profile. The API gateway CORS config will be updated to allow the frontend
origin. The result is a deployable, end-to-end demonstrable internet banking solution.


ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
-------------------
- [x] Login page authenticates via Keycloak and redirects to dashboard on success
- [x] Dashboard shows account balance and last 10 transactions
- [x] Fund transfer form submits and shows success/error feedback
- [x] Utility payment form submits and shows success/error feedback
- [x] User profile page displays current user details
- [x] Logout clears session and returns to login
- [x] All pages are protected (unauthenticated users redirected to login)
- [x] Next.js app builds without errors (npm run build)
- [x] API gateway CORS updated to allow frontend origin


IMPLEMENTATION PLAN
-------------------
1.  Scaffold Next.js 14 app with TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + App Router at `internet-banking-frontend/`
2.  Install and configure NextAuth.js with Keycloak provider
3.  Create auth middleware to protect all routes
4.  Create API client layer (lib/api.ts) that attaches Bearer token to every request via the gateway
5.  Build layout: sidebar nav + header with user avatar + logout
6.  Build login page (NextAuth sign-in redirect)
7.  Build dashboard page: account balance card + recent transactions table
8.  Build fund transfer page: form with from/to account + amount + submit
9.  Build utility payment page: form with provider + account + amount + submit
10. Build user profile page: display user info
11. Update API gateway CORS configuration to allow http://localhost:3000
12. Wire up shadcn/ui components throughout
13. Verify `npm run build` passes
14. Update task to COMPLETE


